  "version": 1,
  "title": "Robust expanders: spanning structures and Hamilton decompositions",
  "abstract": "Seven Lean results on robust expansion. Fixed-cardinality sampling preserves robust out-expansion with an explicit expansion parameter and failure bound. Sufficiently large robust outexpanders of linear minimum semidegree have a Hamilton cycle. Robust graphs of linear minimum degree admit spanning vertex-disjoint paths between prescribed pairs. Almost regular robust graphs admit edge-disjoint realizations of small layouts with a robust remainder. The final three results prove approximate and exact Hamilton decompositions for regular digraphs and exact Hamilton decompositions for even-regular graphs.",
